{
  "title": "Comprehensive Generative AI Market Map & Underserved Opportunity Analysis",
  "content": "This plan builds on the initial research already conducted and decomposes the market mapping into parallel deep-dive research tracks across the key dimensions of the generative AI landscape, followed by a synthesis step that identifies underserved opportunities. Each research track focuses on a distinct MECE segment of the market. The final reasoning task synthesizes all findings into a comprehensive market map with prioritized underserved opportunities.\n\n**Axes:**\n- Uncertainty is moderate (initial research done, but deep segment-level analysis needed)\n- Decomposability is high (market segments are independent)\n- Therefore: join='all' with parallel research tracks + synthesis",
  "tasks": [
    {
      "goal": "Deep-dive into the generative AI infrastructure & foundation model layer: map all major foundation model providers (OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, Meta, Mistral, Cohere, etc.), cloud infrastructure players (AWS, Azure, GCP), GPU/chip companies (NVIDIA, AMD, custom silicon), and model hosting/serving platforms. Identify market concentration, pricing models, and gaps in the infrastructure stack (e.g., affordable inference, edge deployment, specialized hardware for SMEs).",
      "tool_name": "spawn_sub_agent",
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "goal": "Deep-dive into generative AI middleware & developer tooling layer: map MLOps platforms, fine-tuning services, RAG frameworks, vector databases (Pinecone, Weaviate, Chroma, etc.), prompt engineering tools, evaluation/testing frameworks, AI orchestration (LangChain, LlamaIndex), and AI safety/guardrails tools. Identify which sub-segments are crowded vs. underserved, and where developer pain points remain unaddressed.",
      "tool_name": "spawn_sub_agent",
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "goal": "Deep-dive into generative AI application layer by modality: map text generation (content, copywriting, code), image generation (Midjourney, DALL-E, Stable Diffusion, Flux), video generation (Sora, Runway, Kling, Pika), audio/music generation (Suno, Udio, ElevenLabs), 3D/spatial generation, and multi-modal applications. For each modality, identify key players, market maturity, and underserved use cases or quality gaps.",
      "tool_name": "spawn_sub_agent",
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "goal": "Deep-dive into vertical/industry-specific generative AI applications: map adoption and solutions across healthcare (drug discovery, clinical documentation, medical imaging), legal (contract analysis, legal research), finance (risk analysis, reporting, fraud detection), education (tutoring, content creation), manufacturing, agriculture, government, and other verticals. Identify which industries have the least AI penetration and biggest unmet needs, and what regulatory or domain-specific barriers exist.",
      "tool_name": "spawn_sub_agent",
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "goal": "Deep-dive into generative AI trust, safety, compliance & governance layer: map companies and tools addressing AI safety, hallucination detection, content authenticity/watermarking, copyright compliance, data privacy (GDPR/HIPAA-compliant AI), bias detection/mitigation, AI audit trails, regulatory compliance tools, and enterprise governance frameworks. Identify gaps especially for regulated industries, SMEs, and non-English markets.",
      "tool_name": "spawn_sub_agent",
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "goal": "Research the generative AI market from an underserved demographics and geographies perspective: investigate gaps in non-English language AI models, emerging market opportunities (Latin America, Africa, Southeast Asia, Middle East), SME-focused solutions vs. enterprise-only offerings, accessibility tools, and generative AI for non-technical users. Also examine funding patterns to identify where venture capital is NOT flowing despite market need.",
      "tool_name": "spawn_sub_agent",
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "goal": "Synthesize all research from the six parallel tracks into a comprehensive generative AI market map document. Structure it as: (1) Market overview with size estimates and growth projections, (2) Layered market map (infrastructure → middleware → applications → verticals → trust/governance), (3) Competitive landscape heat map showing crowded vs. sparse segments, (4) Top 10-15 ranked underserved opportunities with rationale, estimated market size, barrier analysis, and recommended entry strategies. Present findings in a clear, actionable format.",
